 "construction": "For each held-out annotator a in {0,1,2,3}: human_a = mean over b != a of macroF1(votes[:,b], votes[:,a]); model_a = mean over b != a of macroF1(votes[:,b], model_pred); delta_a = model_a - human_a. Reported as the mean over the four held-out annotators, per stratum.",
 "why_exclude_self": "Scoring an annotator against a reference set that contains themselves makes one of the terms an identity and inflates the human side. Excluding a from the reference costs precision and buys a comparison that is not rigged. The model is scored against the SAME three references so the two sides differ only in who produced the prediction.",
 "verdict_rule": "BELOW THE HUMAN PANEL if the 95% CI on delta excludes 0 below; ABOVE THE HUMAN PANEL if it excludes 0 above; INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM THE HUMAN PANEL if it contains 0.",
 "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "If the model is INDISTINGUISHABLE from the human panel on the contested strata while scoring 26-49 macro F1 there, then the low absolute scores reported in Phase 3 are a property of the task and not of the model. That inference is licensed only for the strata where the verdict is INDISTINGUISHABLE or ABOVE.",
 "interpretation_superseded": "The pre-registration fixed the interpretation 'if the model is INDISTINGUISHABLE from the human panel on the contested strata while scoring 26-49 macro F1, the low absolute scores are a property of the task and not of the model.' That inference is now only PARTLY licensed. The modal-vote oracle added in P6-AMD-5 shows the attainable ceiling on contested images is 0.67, not 1.0, so a large part of the Phase 3 decline IS the ceiling moving -- consistent with the Phase 3B ceiling-normalised analysis. But the model reaches only about a quarter of the way from an individual annotator to that ceiling, so a substantial model shortfall remains and 'the low scores are a property of the task' overstates it. The thesis must use the qualified_verdict field, not verdict_summary.",
